# Go source is written with LF, and the generated files are compared byte for
# byte against what the generator produces. A checkout that rewrites the working
# tree with CRLF, as Git does by default on Windows, would make that comparison
# fail for a reason that has nothing to do with the code.
* text=auto eol=lf

# docs/ holds the documentation and the site that publishes it, and nothing the
# module ships. Counting the site's JavaScript as the language of the repository
# would say the wrong thing about what this is.
docs/** linguist-documentation
